knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3769 (issue https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/issues/3217)
What it fixes: on a Nitro build for a Node-like preset (node, bun), Nitro's static handler is the
first middleware of the app, so a direct request for a `public/` file was answered before the
vinext service ran and middleware never saw it, even when its matcher listed the file (Next.js
deploy test middleware-static-files: `/file.svg`, `/vercel copy.svg`, `/vercel%20copy.svg`,
`/another/file.svg`, `/glob/file.svg`).
The Nitro setup hook now lists the public files the middleware matcher can cover (`has`/`missing`
ignored; no matcher, or one that cannot be read statically, covers every file) and registers a
Nitro runtime plugin that sends a GET/HEAD for one of them to the vinext service, the same
service Nitro's renderer calls. If middleware lets the request continue, vinext fetches the file
back through the Nitro app (the fetcher from vinext-3750); a fetch nested inside a request the
plugin handles reaches the Nitro app unchanged, so the static handler serves it and a rewrite
destination never runs middleware twice. `/_next/static/` build assets and uncovered files keep
Nitro's static fast path. Dev, workerd presets and apps without middleware are unchanged.
Behaviour change: middleware WITHOUT a matcher now runs for every public file on these presets,
as under `next start`.
Port difference: upstream passes a `servesDirectRetrievals` argument from the Nitro Pages branch
that vinext-3750 adds; editing that line here would stop vinext-3750 recognising itself as
applied. Instead the plugin's request store lives on `globalThis`, and the Pages filesystem route
serves a direct public-file request when the store says the plugin forwarded it. The setup
lives in its own Nitro plugin object (vinext:nitro-middleware-public-files) rather than inside
vinext:nitro-route-rules, whose lines vinext-3436/3747/3766 already edit. Same behaviour.
Applies on top of vinext-3750-nitro-public-file-rewrites.patch (depends on its fetcher).
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3769.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

